Algorithm
Start.
Read the number of courses n.
Create a list to store course names and an adjacency list to represent the graph.
Enter the names of all courses.
Read the number of prerequisite links e.
For each link:
Enter the source course and linked course.
Find their corresponding indices.
If both courses exist, add the connection to the adjacency list.
Otherwise, display an invalid course name message.
Display the adjacency list of all courses.
Enter the course name whose linked courses are to be displayed.
Search for the selected course.
If the course exists:
Display its directly linked courses.
If no linked courses exist, display None.
Otherwise, display Course not found!
Stop.

